{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban Electrically Assisted Pedal Cycles from cycle lanes",
        "additional_details": "Current cycle lanes are often too narrow to contain the number of cyclists and EAPCs which can be ridden in such a way as to cause potential danger to non-motorised cyclists. We believe they should be considered motorised vehicles (like motorbikes) and should not be able to use cycle lanes.",
        "background": "We believe Electrically Assisted Pedal cycles (EAPCs) are dangerous in cycle lanes as they can go too fast and are extremely heavy when there is a collision. In our view, they and other motorised modes of transport should not be in cycle lanes.",
